    <span class="tag tag-purple">Architecture</span>
    <span class="tag tag-cyan">Efficiency</span>
    <span class="tag tag-green">Interactive</span>
  </div>
  <h1>Variable-Width Transformers: Why Every Layer Shouldn't Get the Same Budget</h1>
  <p class="lead">Standard transformers give the same hidden dimension to every layer — but MIT's &gt;&lt;former shows this is wasteful. Middle layers routinely collapse their representations to near-zero entropy. A ×-shaped width profile (wide early and late, narrow in the middle) saves 22% pre-training FLOPs under matched-compute scaling, shrinks KV cache by 10–11%, and consistently outperforms parameter-matched baselines from 200M to 2B parameters.</p>
