</section>

<section id="s-residual" data-code="residual">
<div class="section-no">04 — The Fixed-Residual Construction</div>
<h2>How Dimensions Bypass Narrow Layers Without Extra Parameters</h2>
<p>Making layers have different widths raises a practical problem: how do you connect a wide layer to a narrow one? A naive approach would train a projection matrix to downsize the residual — but this adds parameters, changes the residual path, and (empirically) performs worse.</p>
<p>The &gt;&lt;former's key innovation is the <strong>fixed-residual construction</strong>: a single global residual stream is maintained at the width of the <em>widest</em> layer in the model. Each transformer block reads from and writes to only a contiguous <em>slice</em> of this stream — its own layer width. The unused dimensions don't disappear; they <em>bypass</em> the narrow block and are carried forward unchanged.</p>

<div class="vp">
  <div class="vp-head">
    <span class="vp-title">Fixed-residual carry-forward — walk through the mechanism step by step</span>
    <span class="vp-hint">click Next to advance</span>
  </div>
  <div class="vp-body">
    <div class="step-list" id="residual-steps">
      <div class="step-box active">
        <div class="step-num">1</div>
        <div class="step-body">
          <div class="step-title">Wide layer (d=1600) — full residual in use</div>
          <div class="step-desc">All 1600 dimensions of the global residual stream are active. The block reads all dimensions, runs attention + MLP, and writes updated values back to all 1600 positions.</div>
          <div class="step-code">residual[0:1600] → Block → residual[0:1600]</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="step-box">
        <div class="step-num">2</div>
        <div class="step-body">
          <div class="step-title">Narrowing to d=480 — truncate, rest bypass</div>
          <div class="step-desc">The next block only has width 480. It reads residual[0:480], runs attention + MLP on those dimensions, and writes back only to [0:480]. The remaining 1120 dimensions [480:1600] are <strong>not touched</strong> — they pass through unchanged in the global residual.</div>
          <div class="step-code">residual[0:480] → Block → residual[0:480]
residual[480:1600] — bypassed (unchanged) →</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="step-box">
        <div class="step-num">3</div>
        <div class="step-body">
